@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000

### Register: creates a new user account (should return 201; run twice to test duplicate-email handling)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test User",
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### Login: signs in with the account registered above (should return a JWT on success)
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### Me (valid token): uses the token from the login request above (should return 200 with the current user; send Login first)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

### Me (no token): request without an Authorization header (should be rejected with 401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me

### Me (fake token): request with an invalid, unsigned token (should be rejected with 401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer faketoken123
